# Everything in this repository is ultimately read by a Linux container or a Linux CI
# runner, so the working tree must be LF on every platform it is cloned on.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout, the task workspaces are
# copied into containers with those carriage returns intact, and the shell inside reads
# the CR as part of the command:
#
#   vendor/build_repo.sh: 10: set: Illegal option -
#
# where line 10 is a perfectly valid `set -eu`. Five of the twelve tasks ship a shell
# script, so a Windows clone could not run them at all. Found by running the Docker
# backend on a Windows machine, which is the first time anyone had.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Left alone entirely. Git must never rewrite a byte of these: the wheelhouse is a real
# offline package index, the gzipped log is the input to a forensics task whose answer
# depends on its exact contents, and the GIF is the README hero.
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.bundle binary

